            <strong>IECC Climate Zone 4A — 4 full seasons</strong>
            <span>~2,500 sunshine hours per year</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ll-why__copy">
          <p class="ll-kicker">Why LLumar for Philadelphia</p>
          <h2>Philadelphia's Stock of Aging Glass Needs a Film That Works Year-Round</h2>
          <p class="ll-lead">Philadelphia sits in IECC Climate Zone 4A — a mixed-humid zone with genuine winters and genuine summers. LLumar film installer for Philadelphia properties succeeds because the lineup covers both seasons: the ATC Series for summer solar load, and the Low-E Series for winter heat retention on the city's large stock of aging single-pane glass. Add the density of south- and west-facing office glass in Center City, and the precision of LLumar's commercial lineup becomes a real advantage.</p>
          <ul class="ll-checks">
            <li>Single-pane rowhome glass loses heat in winter — LLumar Low-E adds an insulating layer that improves U-value without replacing the window</li>
            <li>Center City offices with south and west glazing face severe solar heat gain — LLumar ATC Series rejects up to 74% of solar energy while maintaining clear views</li>
            <li>Retail properties on busy Philadelphia corridors benefit from LLumar's safety film to delay forced entry and retain glass fragments during impact</li>
            <li>All LLumar architectural films are NFRC-certified — independently rated for VLT, SHGC, and U-value</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="ll-link-copy">"LLumar architectural window film is engineered to meet the performance demands of commercial buildings in every climate zone," according to LLumar. For broader energy improvement options, see our <a href="/benefits/energy-savings/">energy savings window film</a> page. Properties with security concerns may also benefit from our <a href="/benefits/safety-and-security/">safety and security window film</a> service. For the full commercial portfolio, explore our <a href="/applications/office/">commercial office window film</a> applications. See the full <a href="https://www.llumar.com/en/commercial-window-film/solar/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LLumar commercial solar control film</a> lineup.</p>
          <div class="ll-climate">
            <span><strong>2,500</strong> Sunshine hours per year</span>
            <span><strong>87°F</strong> Average July high</span>
            <span><strong>Zone 4A</strong> Mixed-humid, 4 seasons</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ll-slider" id="llSlider" aria-label="Residential and commercial LLumar window film uses">
      <div class="ll-slider__track" id="llTrack">
        <article class="ll-slider__slide is-active" data-slide="0">
          <img src="/images/llumar-window-film-philadelphia-residential.jpg" alt="Philadelphia rowhome living room with LLumar residential window film" title="LLumar residential window film for Philadelphia rowhomes" class="ll-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="ll-slider__shade"></div>
          <div class="ll-slider__content">
            <span class="ll-slider__step">01</span>
            <h2>Philadelphia Rowhomes. LLumar Precision.</h2>
            <p>Philadelphia's housing stock runs heavily on single-pane glass — beautiful to look through, poor for heat retention in winter and solar control in summer. LLumar Low-E and ATC films are engineered for this: one insulates, one rejects heat, and both preserve the original window. Authorized LLumar installation can address both concerns without window replacement.</p>
            <div class="ll-slider__faq">
              <details>
                <summary>Which LLumar film is best for Philadelphia rowhomes?</summary>
                <p>For year-round performance including winter insulation, LLumar Low-E is the standard recommendation. For summer heat and glare on south- or west-facing windows, the ATC Series delivers up to 74% solar rejection. We assess your glass and orientation before recommending.</p>
              </details>
              <details>
                <summary>Will LLumar film change how my home looks from the street?</summary>
                <p>Most LLumar residential films are optically clear or very lightly reflective — virtually undetectable at street level. We show you samples before any installation.</p>
              </details>
              <details>
                <summary>Can LLumar film go on historic or single-pane glass?</summary>
                <p>Yes. LLumar makes specific series approved for single-pane glass, including the aging wavy glass common in Philadelphia rowhomes. We evaluate glass type and condition before installation.</p>
              </details>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ll-slider__slide" data-slide="1">
          <img src="/images/llumar-window-film-philadelphia-commercial.jpg" alt="Center City commercial office with LLumar ATC solar control window film" title="LLumar commercial window film for Philadelphia offices" class="ll-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="ll-slider__shade"></div>
          <div class="ll-slider__content">
            <span class="ll-slider__step">02</span>
            <h2>Philadelphia Offices. LLumar Performance.</h2>
            <p>Center City high-rises, Old City storefronts, and University City campuses all face the same problem — too much glass, too much solar heat, and HVAC systems working overtime. LLumar ATC Series solar control film reduces cooling load by rejecting up to 74% of solar energy. Payback periods for commercial LLumar window film Philadelphia installations typically average 2–4 years through HVAC savings.</p>
            <div class="ll-slider__faq">
              <details>
                <summary>How quickly does LLumar film pay back on commercial buildings?</summary>
                <p>Most commercial installations with significant south- or west-facing glass see payback within 2–4 years through HVAC savings alone. Larger glass footprints and high utility costs accelerate that timeline.</p>
              </details>
              <details>
                <summary>Will installation disrupt our operations?</summary>
                <p>Minimal disruption. Our crews work floor by floor and can schedule evenings or weekends for occupied commercial spaces. We coordinate with building management on every project.</p>
              </details>
              <details>
                <summary>Does LLumar ATC film work on curtain wall and floor-to-ceiling glass?</summary>
                <p>Yes — large commercial glass is where LLumar film delivers its biggest results. Film is applied in panels with nearly invisible seams and performs consistently across curtain wall systems and storefront glass.</p>
              </details>
            </div>
          </div>
